From 795582435b5a8f02a96984c33dc1ef712e30c752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:39:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: fold the GDN q/k l2 norms into the decode conv-fold
 epilogue (+1.3% decode, byte-exact)

qwen35moe convolves [q | k | v] as one 8192-channel block and then l2-normalises
the q and k halves per 128-wide head. Grouped since 0019 that is still 30
launches per token at 2.0 us, and every one of them re-reads 16 KB the conv fold
had in registers a moment earlier. A 256-thread conv block owns exactly 256
channels, which is exactly two 128-wide norm rows, so warps 0 and 1 can replay
the stock one-warp l2_norm body out of shared memory: same
"col = lane; col += 32" accumulation order, the same warp_reduce_sum (for
block_size == WARP_SIZE, block_reduce<SUM,32> IS warp_reduce_sum), the same
rsqrtf(fmaxf(tmp, eps*eps)) and the same store order. Byte-identical to
l2_norm_f32_grouped, 30 fewer launches per token.

Getting the kernel right was the easy half. Where the result is allowed to land
was the round, exactly as in 0032 and 0037:

1. With separate destinations ggml-alloc hands the two norms buffers that a node
   between the conv and the norms is still using, and the fold declines on every
   layer. So the norms are made IN-PLACE on the conv output at the decode shape
   (qwen35moe.cpp, GGML_L2_NORM_INPLACE=0 restores). That is semantically free -
   the q and k halves of the conv output have no consumer other than these two
   norms - and it puts the result inside the buffer the fold already owns. Only
   at n_t == 1: at prefill the q/k views are strided over tokens and an in-place
   destination would make the norm kernel store contiguously into a strided view.
2. In place, the norm destination then overlaps the ACTIVATION, because at the
   decode shape ggml-alloc routinely co-locates the two (the CONCAT is the
   activation last consumer). That is not a new hazard: the fold already depends
   on the co-location being exact, since thread ch reads x[ch] and then writes
   y[ch], the same address. The norm write lands on the same 256 channels the
   block has already read, after a __syncthreads, so it is safe under exactly
   that condition - x->data == silu->data and a unit channel stride - and the
   detector declines on anything weaker.

The CONCAT output is deliberately NOT in the operand guard: when this fold fires
the concat is never materialised, and the 0031 detector has already rejected any
consumer of it other than the SSM_CONV and the writeback CPY, both folded away.
Its buffer is dead, and ggml-alloc hands it to the norm destinations on every
layer - guarding on it declines the whole fold for nothing.

The epilogue lives in a separate kernel (ssm_conv_fold_l2_f32) rather than a
runtime branch inside ssm_conv_fold_stock_f32; see 0040 for what a not-taken
branch in a hot kernel costs. GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SSM_CONV_L2_FOLD=1 restores the
separate grouped launch; GGML_CUDA_SSM_CONV_L2_DBG=1 prints accept/decline.

Measured (runner box, HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0, whole-process interleaved 3-arm
A/B against a control binary built from the parent commit, rotated order):

- tg128: control 145.36-145.79 (median 145.65), fold+inplace OFF 145.57-145.80
  (median 145.63, ratio 0.9999), ON 147.50-147.80 (median 147.58, ratio 1.0133);
  arms disjoint 5/5, min(ON) 147.50 > max(control) 145.79
- pp512 neutral: 6 further rounds at r=3, per-round ratios 0.9988-1.0039,
  median 0.9997
- tg128 @ d16384 134.01 -> 135.84 (+1.37%), @ d32768 124.53 -> 126.07 (+1.24%)
- decode census: 781.1 -> 751.1 dispatches/token, 5680 -> 5627 us of kernel;
  l2_norm_f32_grouped gone, the conv fold 1.57 -> 2.24 us
- decode-path ppl -b 512 -ub 1 --chunks 8: 3.9338 all on, 3.9338 with fold and
  inplace off, 3.9338 with inplace on and fold off - identical to four decimals
  in all three arms, and identical to the banked stack
- gate-shape ppl -c 512 --chunks 8: 3.9271, unchanged (neither half fires there)
- llama-server greedy 6/6 BYTE-EXACT vs the fold-off control
- test-backend-ops L2_NORM / SSM_CONV / GATED_DELTA_NET OK
